1
00:00:00,118 --> 00:00:05,380
Every time we use AI, it feels like we are talking to something which knows everything.

2
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:06,281
But we're not.

3
00:00:06,281 --> 00:00:11,943
We are talking to a machine which uses billions of numbers making calculated guesses.

4
00:00:11,943 --> 00:00:15,324
And every word we talk to AI cost us money.

5
00:00:15,404 --> 00:00:18,085
So, how this all actually works?

6
00:00:18,365 --> 00:00:22,767
AI is a machine that learns patterns from huge amounts of data.

7
00:00:22,847 --> 00:00:26,008
An AI model is the brain of this machine.

8
00:00:26,089 --> 00:00:30,210
And this system built entirely on mathematics.

9
00:00:30,454 --> 00:00:35,558
Inside this brain, there are billions of numbers which are called parameters.

10
00:00:35,558 --> 00:00:39,220
These parameters store everything the model has learned.

11
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:47,665
And based on these parameters, AI decides what to say next, what image to generate, or
what actions to take.

12
00:00:47,806 --> 00:00:49,994
But here is something very interesting.

13
00:00:49,994 --> 00:00:52,909
AI cannot read full words like we do.

14
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:57,232
It breaks everything into tiny pieces called tokens.

15
00:00:57,232 --> 00:00:59,864
For instance, word understand becomes

16
00:00:59,864 --> 00:01:02,776
Two tokens under plus stand.

17
00:01:02,776 --> 00:01:07,700
Even the simple sentences like I love choice become three tokens.

18
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:09,841
I plus love plus choice.

19
00:01:09,841 --> 00:01:16,366
So when we type in the AI chat box, AI is not reading words, it is reading tokens.

20
00:01:16,366 --> 00:01:19,188
These tokens are then converted to numbers.

21
00:01:19,188 --> 00:01:25,392
These numbers travel through many layers inside the AI model, something called neural
network.

22
00:01:25,552 --> 00:01:28,334
First layer, look for simple things.

23
00:01:28,362 --> 00:01:33,184
Next layer finds the patterns and the next layer understands the bigger idea.

24
00:01:33,184 --> 00:01:37,165
Step by step every answer has become clearer.

25
00:01:37,386 --> 00:01:40,387
Each connection has its own strength.

26
00:01:40,387 --> 00:01:44,489
A number that decides how strong the signal should be.

27
00:01:44,609 --> 00:01:48,591
During training, the model keeps guessing the next token.

28
00:01:48,591 --> 00:01:51,912
If it is wrong, it adjusts its strength.

29
00:01:51,912 --> 00:01:57,534
Then it tries again and again and billion more times until it is right.

30
00:01:57,856 --> 00:02:03,308
Once training is done, model is frozen and now it is ready to answer us.

31
00:02:03,308 --> 00:02:05,949
This stage is called inference.

32
00:02:06,090 --> 00:02:14,273
When we use AI like ChatGPT, Copilot, or Cloud AI, our messages go to a computer called a
server.

33
00:02:14,613 --> 00:02:16,994
The server runs the model for us.

34
00:02:17,274 --> 00:02:22,117
And here's something interesting: model doesn't count tokens, the server does.

35
00:02:22,117 --> 00:02:23,737
Server counts the tokens.

36
00:02:23,737 --> 00:02:25,664
How many tokens we send?

37
00:02:25,664 --> 00:02:28,657
And how many tokens AI sends back to us?

38
00:02:28,657 --> 00:02:30,698
And we are charged for both.

39
00:02:30,698 --> 00:02:41,928
For instance, if we have 200 tokens as an input and AI replies back with 500 tokens as
output, we pay for 700 tokens in total.

40
00:02:41,928 --> 00:02:47,853
And here's the catch: many companies charge more for output tokens than input tokens.

41
00:02:47,853 --> 00:02:51,596
So long answers equal higher cost.

42
00:02:51,596 --> 00:02:54,178
If AI responds with long stories,

43
00:02:54,178 --> 00:02:59,842
Detailed explanations or larger codes, token usage explodes.

44
00:02:59,862 --> 00:03:07,167
Even our conversation history we had with AI adds tokens every time we continue chatting
with the model.

45
00:03:07,227 --> 00:03:12,831
This is why cloud AI feels cheap at first but becomes expensive over time.

46
00:03:12,891 --> 00:03:16,353
So, how can we avoid these token charges?

47
00:03:16,393 --> 00:03:19,595
Local AI models run on our computers.

48
00:03:19,956 --> 00:03:23,528
No server, no tracking, no billing.

49
00:03:23,779 --> 00:03:30,059
What it means, we can now generate unlimited tokens from AI for free.

50
00:03:30,059 --> 00:03:36,051
AI doesn't know everything, it is doing calculated guess for what comes next.

51
00:03:36,051 --> 00:03:38,833
And every guess has a cost.

